Music-Analytics
A personal music analytics API that ingests data from Last.fm, built as a learning lab for backend architecture, REST, GraphQL, and database design.

The project is structured around evolutionary architecture. The system will be rebuilt three times across different communication paradigms to compare performance, DX (developer experience), and architectural trade-offs:

V1: REST API (Express, Prisma, SQLite) — Current Phase
V2: GraphQL API (Apollo Server / Nexus)
V3: Serverless / Cloud Functions
The domain model, business rules, and analytical queries remain constant, while the delivery mechanism changes.

🛠️ Tech Stack (V1)
Runtime: Node.js
Language: TypeScript (Strict Mode)
Web Framework: Express
Database ORM: Prisma
Database: SQLite (local file-based SQL for prototyping)
Database Design
The data ingestion pipeline parses raw JSON from the Last.fm API and normalizes it into a relational schema:

User: Stores user metadata.
Artist: Unique registry of artists.
Track: Unique registry of tracks, linked to an Artist (handles same-name tracks by different artists via compound keys).
Scrobble: Represents a single playback event connecting a User and a Track at a specific timestamp.
